            <ArticleTitle>[Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty, x-ray contrast researches and contrast-induced nephropathy in geriatrics].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>511-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The state-of-the-art review of literature on the problem of percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty in patients of senior age groups with sharp cardiovascular pathology is submitted in three parts. In the second part the review of epidemiology and risk factors of the contrast-induced nephropathy emergence in intervention gerontocardiology is submitted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
